Z||000000||GTDusty||10-28-2001||10:56 PM|||| I was cleaning my car and noticed a plug lookin thing on the passenger side just under the dash on the right side. It was just in front of the sub-woofer and looks like something was supposed to be plugged in there. What is that?<P> Dusty||||reg||11
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-28-2001||11:05 PM||||Probably the blue "dingy" thing that a lot of people remove.  Does your car "chime" at you if you leave your headlights on when you remove the keys from the ignition?  If not (and if there is no rectangular blue thing under your dash) then you are "dingy-less"!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDusty||10-28-2001||11:13 PM|||| I have no dingy; dingy-less; I am WITHOUT dingy.<P> Life sux without a dingy<BR>Dusty||||reg||9
Z||000003||theogre||10-28-2001||11:36 PM||||there is an article in my cave that explains the major reason why they get yanked. I didn't like not having the dingy thingy when mine broke.<P>The new style chime boxes have a defect from the factory. It can be fixed once you know where to look.<P>I wanted mine to work because I often lock the headlights up in winter weather. Durring the daytime you don't always realize you've left them on if the chime isn't working. The switch doesn't provide the visual que that the old pull out style ones did. The rocker looks nearly the same on or off.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rick 88||10-29-2001||08:35 AM||||Dusty,<P>Don't go dingy-less! Try a local wrecking yard. I'm sure you can find a dingy there. Since they are mounted under the dash they are rarely removed and usually good. You will be looking for a light blue box. It can be a little irritating at times but is a good reminder. My handbrake also activated the dingy when it is applied.<P>Where is Granbury located?<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTDusty||10-29-2001||08:20 PM||||  I see the spot where the rectangle dingy box goes...but where Im talking about is right in the corner of the door,dash, and floor carpet. Kinda just under the front lip of the dash when you lookunder. It is round and almost looks like a light might have gone there or something. Anyway..its round and not as far under as the dingy thingy.<P> Dusty<P> BTW. Granbury is about an hour south of Ft Worth||||reg||11
Z||000006||mrfiero||10-29-2001||08:29 PM||||In that case it is probably the under dash lights that you are missing.  Not all Fieros came with these.....I believe it was part of an option group.<P>When you open your doors or turn the dimmer up (to turn on the overhead lights) does a light come on under each side of the dash? <P>If not and if there is not bulb/socket in the bracket (which sounds like what you are describing), then you do not have these lights.<P>The good news is these are pretty simple to install if you just have to have them.  All it takes is the harness (separate from the main harness) from a Fiero that came with the under dash lights.  There is a plug that plugs into the fuse junction block (behind main fuse panel) and then the two sockets that attach into the brackets under the dash.  ALl Fieros have these brackets, since that is also the main attachment point for the dash itself.  The hardest part is running the harness under the dash.  The "proper" way is to remove the dash, but you don't necessarily need to do this to make it functional. <P>I might have one of these harnesses lying around.......LMK if you want it.||||reg||1
